&lt;p&gt;Current URL(s):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/fontfont/ff_isonorm/" title="http://www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/fontfont/ff_isonorm/"&gt;http://www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/fontfont/ff_isonorm/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/elsner_flake/isonorm/" title="http://www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/elsner_flake/isonorm/"&gt;http://www.fontshop.com/fonts/downloads/elsner_flake/isonorm/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designed by &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Robert%20Kirchner"&gt;Robert Kirchner&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Even before &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/typophile.com/wiki/AutoCAD"&gt;AutoCAD&lt;/a&gt; decided to acknowledge the existence of &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/typophile.com/wiki/PostScript"&gt;PostScript&lt;/a&gt;, artists and designers have been asking for a &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016034020/http:/typophile.com/wiki/PostScript"&gt;PostScript&lt;/a&gt; version of the Isonorm draughtsman&amp;rsquo;s face. A lot of creative people are eagerly waiting to misuse this geometrically-constructed standard letterform for their free-wheeling design. So now, at last, you can have some fun.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>